e give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Return rating echoing its id exactly. Provide lines.\n\nWill output:\n\nid: P2167\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 3\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: The ledger provides secure lifetime storage and integrity for logs, which contributes to meeting Article 12 record-keeping but does not itself ensure automatic event capture or content relevance. Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: Centralizing immutable logs directly addresses the mandate to technically allow automatic recording and keep logs available over system lifetime. Score 4.\n\nAcceptability evidence: A hardened write-once database with restricted access and cryptographic hashing is a common, norm-compliant compliance practice. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Deploying a dedicated time-series cluster with cross-region archival requires nontrivial engineering and cloud resources but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab. Score 3.\n\nOriginality evidence: Centralized immutable audit ledgers for compliance logging are a common, well-known infrastructure pattern. Score 1.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The proposal treats compliance as standard logging practice with new tools but leaves the lab’s R&D workflow and its relationship to compliance unchanged. Score 1.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
