sparent during failure events and audit post-hoc to identify substantial modifications or risks. Does that meet Article 12 requirements? Article 12 requires recording events logs over lifetime, identifying situations risk, facilitate post-market monitoring, etc., and for specific systems: period of use, reference database, input data match, identification of natural persons. High-dimensional latent snapshots may not directly provide those required fields, but could help identify risks. It contributes partially but may not fully meet mandate. Effectiveness maybe 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution, partial. Could be 4? If you could do it, would it solve main problem? Logging mandate requires specific logs; explainable logs of internal state may be extra but not guarantee compliance with required fields. So partial.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree idea clearly applies to stated problem. 4 = solves identified problem directly related. 3 = solves implied problem related. 2 = may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates.\n\nProposal directly addresses logging mandate by creating logs for audit to identify modifications/risks. So applies directly. I'd say 4.\n\nNow output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale in order: give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating... Probably output lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2411\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 3\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nEnsure each evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.\n\n",
