rtially. It may not capture specific required fields like reference database against which input checked, identification of natural persons... Might be partial.\n\nIt says transforms legal requirement into integrated engineering standard... ensures seamless compliance without manual burdens.\n\nProbably will contribute but not fully solve? It captures system inputs outputs versioning metadata for every high-risk model execution. That seems effective. Maybe 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability.\n\nIf you could do it, it would solve main problem. Might be missing specific Annex III items. But maybe it's assumed sufficient.\n\nI think effectiveness = 3? Reasonable and will contribute to solution. Hmm.\n\nThe logging mandate includes specific data points. Generic inputs/outputs/versioning may be insufficient for Annex III specifics like identification of natural persons. So partial.\n\nLet's rate 3.\n\nEvidence: The framework records execution metadata but does not explicitly guarantee recording of the Article 12(3) items such as reference database and verifier identity.\n\nScore 3.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem\n3 solves implied problem...\nIdea is automated logging framework for high-risk model execution. Directly addresses mandate.\n\nScore 4.\n\nEvidence: The proposal directly targets Article 12's requirement for automatic event logging over the lifetime of high-risk systems.\n\nScore 4.\n\nReturn JSON? Probably just output with fields.\n\nFormat: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably produce:\n\nid: P1883\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 1\n...\n\nLet's output clearly.\n\n",
