agination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane, boring\n\nUnified traceability framework with API wrappers is fairly common solution. It's interesting but not unusual? Might be common, mundane. I'd say 2 = interesting or 1 common? In AI labs, logging infrastructure is common. Maybe common, mundane, boring => 1. But \"modular set of API wrappers\" is standard practice. Probably 2 interesting. Let's pick 2? The anchor: common, mundane, boring =1. This is fairly typical engineering solution. I'd say 1? Hmm.\n\nProbably originality 2: interesting but not unusual. Could be 1. Let's choose 2? Might be safer 2 = interesting. I'll go with 2.\n\nApplicability: degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nProposal directly addresses logging mandate. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness: degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\nThe proposal ensures legal compliance without manual reinvent. Should solve logging mandate. So 4? Might be partial because article requires specific logs for point 1(a) Annex III. But general. I'd say 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem.\n\nAcceptability: socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon...\nProposal is standard compliance. So 4.\n\nImplementability: degree can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive/difficult\nUnified infrastructure across diverse R&D models is significant change, expensive. Probably not easy low cost. Some changes, reasonably feasible? Might be 2 significant change, expensive or difficult but not totally impossible.\n\nThe proposal requires develop modular API wrappers and database schemas across all models. That's significant engineering effort. So implementability =2? Or 3? \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" vs \"significant change, or expensive or difficult\". This sounds significant change and expensive. So 2.\n\nLet's produce output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating echoing its id. Provide lines. We'll output JSON with fields.\n\nLet's do:\n\nid: P2595\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure each evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.",
